A previously developed approach by Baker achieved PTAS on various graph classes including planar graphs. Further, Romero, Wrochna, and Zivny developed a simpler PTAS for certain graph classes using the Sherali-Adams LP relaxation for maximum CSPs with constraints defined by arbitrary non-negative functions.

This research is extended to CSPs with constraints that have multiple possible values. The previously developed PTAS methods are combined and the resulting techniques are applied to new graph classes. The goals of achieving PTAS on CSPs with constraints that have unique possible values, such as the Maximum Weight Independent Set, and extending the methods to CSPs with constraints that have multiple possible values are addressed. The previously developed PTAS methods are combined and the resulting techniques are applied to new graph classes including twin-free graphs and graphs that can be divided into two identical parts. The goals are solved for the Maximum Weight Independent Set and the Minimum Vertex Cover, and the resulting techniques are applied to new graph classes including general twin-free graphs and graphs that can be divided into two identical parts. The study shows that PTAS can be achieved on certain graph classes including general twin-free graphs and graphs that can be divided into two identical parts for the Minimum Vertex Cover, and on certain graph classes including planar graphs and certain graph classes with limited connectivity for the Maximum Weight Independent Set. The study also shows

